{#
  The year-at-a-glance timeline.

  Items come from the CANONICAL event records via src/_data/eventListing.js —
  never from homepage copy — so the timeline, the events listing and the detail
  pages cannot disagree about a date, a venue or a title. Dates are generated by
  the same deterministic formatter the other two use.

  THE MOST RECENT FIVE, WHATEVER YEAR THEY BELONG TO.

  This used to read the current academic year's bucket, which meant the band
  emptied itself the moment Site settings moved to a year nobody had added
  events to yet: the homepage went blank while the events page was still full.
  Reading across every year makes that changeover invisible — a new year's
  events arrive at the top as they are added and push the oldest off the end,
  one at a time.

  The homepage is still not an archive. The events page is, and it shows every
  year in its own section.

  "See all events" sits under the timeline in every state — five events, one, or
  none — because an event that fell off the bottom is exactly when somebody
  needs the way through to the full list.

  `.timeline-progress` is the animated rail js/main.js drives; `.tl-item.reveal`
  is what the IntersectionObserver watches. Neither is optional markup.

  Titles use `timeline_title` where the live homepage genuinely differs from the
  event title (all five do — they are short venue-flavoured labels), falling back
  to the resolved title otherwise.

  Expects: eventListing, locale, c, t
#}
{#- NO YEAR BEHIND THIS BAND.

    It used to carry the configured season as a watermark, which was honest
    while the band showed one season. It now shows the most recent five events
    whatever year they belong to, so a single year printed across them says
    something untrue — most visibly at a changeover, where a large "2026/27"
    sat behind five events from 2025/26.

    The events page still labels every year, which is where that information
    belongs: each section owns its own heading and its own watermark. -#}
<section class="section tex-light">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head center reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">{{ c.timeline_eyebrow }}</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">{{ c.timeline_title.lead }} <span class="fancy">{{ c.timeline_title.fancy }}</span></h2>
    </div>
{#- ACROSS EVERY YEAR, not the current one. See src/_data/eventListing.js:
    reading only the current bucket emptied the homepage the moment Site
    settings moved to a year with no events in it yet. -#}
{%- set homeEvents = eventListing.all | homepageEvents %}
{%- if homeEvents.length %}
    <div class="timeline">
      <div class="timeline-progress" aria-hidden="true"></div>
{%- for event in homeEvents %}
{%- set ec = event[locale.code] %}
      <div class="tl-item reveal">
        <span class="tl-date">{{ event | eventDisplayDate(locale.code) }}</span>
        {#- Relative on purpose: from /pl/ this opens the Polish detail page. -#}
        <h3><a href="event-{{ event.slug }}.html">{{ ec.timeline_title | default(ec | eventTitle) }}</a></h3>
        <p>{{ ec.timeline_summary }}</p>
      </div>
{%- endfor %}
    </div>
{%- else %}
    {#- There is no homepage-visible event ANYWHERE in the collection — not
        merely none in the current year. The heading stays and a concise line
        replaces the items; "See all events" below points at the events page
        either way. -#}
    <p class="lead center">{{ t.home.emptySeason }}</p>
{%- endif %}
    {#- Relative on purpose: from /pl/ this resolves to the Polish events page. -#}
    <div class="center" style="margin-top: 24px;">
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="events.html">{{ t.home.allEventsLabel }}</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
